<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mwaant Yaav</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mwaant Yaav (also written <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwata-yamvo">Mwata Yamvo</a>) is the title of the paramount ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, taken by each king from the late seventeenth century onwards. The Mwaant Yaav and the nobility controlled the trade in salt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and received tribute from subordinate chiefs, who raised military forces under his authority. The title survives today as that of the Lunda paramount chief.</p></div>
